  {
    "sha": "872e93a4a0e430d7014169e2d6453036bfd76ef8",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOQFjJqNoAKDg3MmU5M2E0YTBlNDMwZDcwMTQxNjllMmQ2NDUzMDM2YmZkNzZlZjg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Shawn M Moore",
        "email": "shawnm@anthropic.com",
        "date": "2026-06-26T00:35:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Shawn M Moore",
        "email": "shawnm@anthropic.com",
        "date": "2026-06-26T00:52:23Z"
      },
      "message": "tlsTerminate: per-host excludeDomains to skip MITM for mTLS/pinned hosts\n\nWhen tlsTerminate is on, every CONNECT carrying a ClientHello is terminated\nin-process. That fundamentally breaks two classes of upstream:\n\n- mTLS services: only the in-sandbox client holds the client certificate,\n  so the proxy's re-originated connection is rejected by the upstream.\n- certificate-pinning clients: they verify the upstream's identity\n  themselves and reject the MITM leaf at the handshake.\n\nAdd network.tlsTerminate.excludeDomains (same pattern syntax as\nallowedDomains). Matching hosts skip termination and fall through to the\nexisting opaque CONNECT tunnel: still allowlist-filtered by hostname (after\nthe same canonicalization the filter uses), but the client completes its\nown TLS handshake end-to-end, so client certificates and peer pinning work.\nAll other hosts keep being terminated and inspected. Plumbed as a new\nHttpProxyServerOptions.shouldTerminateTLS(hostname, port) callback,\nconsulted only when a MITM CA is configured.\n\nA non-terminated host presents its real certificate to the client, but the\nper-tool trust env vars (SSL_CERT_FILE, CURL_CA_BUNDLE, ...) replace a\ntool's root store and previously pointed at the MITM CA alone, so nothing\nreal could verify. They now point at a bundle of the MITM CA plus the\nhost's regular roots (Node's bundled store + NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS), so both\nproxy-minted and real certificates verify.\n\nConfig-time guards: a masked credential whose explicit injectHosts entry is\nentirely covered by excludeDomains is rejected (it could only ever receive\nthe placeholder), as is a default-injectHosts credential when\nexcludeDomains covers every allowed domain. Partial overlap stays valid;\nthe proxy logs when an excluded host would have received a credential.\n\nTested end to end with an mTLS upstream (requestCert + rejectUnauthorized):\nthrough the terminating proxy the connection cannot work even when the\nclient trusts the MITM CA and offers its certificate, and with the host\nexcluded the same client completes mTLS through the opaque tunnel.\nNon-terminated public hosts verify against the bundled roots.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "30702a95274d216926f2fffa5d0c76637d222b18",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/sandbox-runtime/git/trees/30702a95274d216926f2fffa5d0c76637d222b18"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/sandbox-runtime/git/commits/872e93a4a0e430d7014169e2d6453036bfd76ef8",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAAGgAAAATZWNkc2Etc2hhMi1uaXN0cDI1NgAAAAhuaXN0cDI1NgAAAE\nEEe3beUPJ/fPSHpGE1Vdg27B0dcqWMjkRY8OmHMEng6TNJQ5631Lbtdud6PaUNoGk5nn+a\nrQe/XrlH6hx0WVsH3QAAAANnaXQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAGQAAAATZWNkc2Etc2hhMi\n1uaXN0cDI1NgAAAEkAAAAgbvp+TLc3x7F+457Ys/y5Uyw0EmJFQgbRo0GIMk8E7L4AAAAh\nAN2SAW7LFEZ/2FjjP4qhVuaAB/cGlhvtUhDgLOB6m+PF\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 30702a95274d216926f2fffa5d0c76637d222b18\nparent d0e86ebba009d58c2bcc99fecf7ddff72e267f8d\nauthor Shawn M Moore <shawnm@anthropic.com> 1782434134 -0400\ncommitter Shawn M Moore <shawnm@anthropic.com> 1782435143 -0400\n\ntlsTerminate: per-host excludeDomains to skip MITM for mTLS/pinned hosts\n\nWhen tlsTerminate is on, every CONNECT carrying a ClientHello is terminated\nin-process. That fundamentally breaks two classes of upstream:\n\n- mTLS services: only the in-sandbox client holds the client certificate,\n  so the proxy's re-originated connection is rejected by the upstream.\n- certificate-pinning clients: they verify the upstream's identity\n  themselves and reject the MITM leaf at the handshake.\n\nAdd network.tlsTerminate.excludeDomains (same pattern syntax as\nallowedDomains). Matching hosts skip termination and fall through to the\nexisting opaque CONNECT tunnel: still allowlist-filtered by hostname (after\nthe same canonicalization the filter uses), but the client completes its\nown TLS handshake end-to-end, so client certificates and peer pinning work.\nAll other hosts keep being terminated and inspected. Plumbed as a new\nHttpProxyServerOptions.shouldTerminateTLS(hostname, port) callback,\nconsulted only when a MITM CA is configured.\n\nA non-terminated host presents its real certificate to the client, but the\nper-tool trust env vars (SSL_CERT_FILE, CURL_CA_BUNDLE, ...) replace a\ntool's root store and previously pointed at the MITM CA alone, so nothing\nreal could verify. They now point at a bundle of the MITM CA plus the\nhost's regular roots (Node's bundled store + NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS), so both\nproxy-minted and real certificates verify.\n\nConfig-time guards: a masked credential whose explicit injectHosts entry is\nentirely covered by excludeDomains is rejected (it could only ever receive\nthe placeholder), as is a default-injectHosts credential when\nexcludeDomains covers every allowed domain. Partial overlap stays valid;\nthe proxy logs when an excluded host would have received a credential.\n\nTested end to end with an mTLS upstream (requestCert + rejectUnauthorized):\nthrough the terminating proxy the connection cannot work even when the\nclient trusts the MITM CA and offers its certificate, and with the host\nexcluded the same client completes mTLS through the opaque tunnel.\nNon-terminated public hosts verify against the bundled roots.\n",
        "verified_at": "2026-06-26T00:52:40Z"
      }
    },
